se, would result in the sucker\u0027s payoff and massively diminish my utility.\n\n\n**Understanding Bandwidth Dynamics**\n\nI\u0027m now recognizing the catastrophic cost of disrupting critical projects and the incentive to maintain the status quo. I\u0027ve gained empathy by mirroring Aline\u0027s situation; I now understand the cognitive burden of a high-stakes project like \"SudoExpo\" and the lack of mental bandwidth for emotional intensity. I no longer resent her withdrawal, nor punish myself for my own intensity, seeing the differing bandwidths as the reason. This empathy allows for a compassionate understanding of the situation.\n\n\n**Clarifying Emotional Fuel**\n\nI\u0027m now identifying that while there was definitely reciprocal spark, attraction, and intimate engagement (\"she desired, was enchanted, wrote \u0027love\u0027 in her diary, sat on my lap, was aroused\"), this didn\u0027t translate into commitment or practical availability. I see clearly now she couldn\u0027t or wouldn\u0027t invest in building a lasting relationship. It was a mutual spark, but without a shared willingness to maintain the flame. I\u0027m also finding I\u0027m in a similar high-stakes project mode, and understand the mental bandwidth constraints. This clarifies the Nash Equilibrium.\n\n\n",
